#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "Distribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the beginning of the game, countries are distributed to all the players. "
"Each country contain one army (represented by an infantryman) at this "
"moment. Each player has some armies to distribute to his countries at her "
"turn (indicated by the presence of her name and her flag in the status bar). "
"Note that five armies are represented by a cavalryman and 10 by a cannon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To put an army on one of your countries, click on it with the left mouse "
"button. To remove an army, click with the right button. Note, as a general "
"rule, that you will never be able to remove more armies than the number you "
"already put."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Placing armies</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Placing armies</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a player has distributed all her armies, the next player is "
"automatically selected to do the same task. When all players have finished "
"to distribute their armies, there is two possibilities that can be selected "
"by two buttons showed in the right panel:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "Redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ": Redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One player wants to change some of his choices. The first player can then "
"remove an army he just put in a country with the right mouse button and put "
"it in another one with the left mouse button. When he finish, he gives "
"control to next player with the 'Valid' button. When all players have "
"finished their redistribution, the two buttons are displayed again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "End of redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ": End of redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "The redistribution is finished and the game can continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the redistribution, a game turn can start. Each player plays at his "
"turn. He has the choice to:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "Next player"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid ": Give hand to the next player (button in the toolbar)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The turn of the current player finishes and it's the turn of the next one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "Attack 1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&nbsp;<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"attackTwo.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Attack 2</phrase> </"
"textobject> </inlinemediaobject> &nbsp;<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"attackThree.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>Attack 3</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> : "
"Attack with one, two or three armies &nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "Attack auto"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To attack, drag with the mouse from the attacking country and drop to the "
"attacked one. You will then be presented with a contextual menu showing the "
"above entries. <screenshot> <screeninfo>Attack menu</screeninfo> "
"<mediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"attackmenu.png\" format="
"\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Attack menu</phrase> </"
"textobject> </mediaobject> </screenshot> For a country X to attack a country "
"Y with x armies, 2 conditions must be fullfilled: 1. the two countries must "
"be neighbours; 2. country X must have at least x+1 armies before the attack. "
"If the attack is valid, a dialog is displayed if necessary for the defender "
"to choose if he wants to defend with one or two armies or let the computer "
"decide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The defender choice done, the fight will happen and be solved. This will "
"described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Defense dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Defense dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move armies"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid ": Move Armies from one country to another"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the last action of a player's turn. It gives the possibility to move "
"some armies from one of his country to another, neighbour of the first one. "
"To choose the two countries, please drag'n drop as for an attack. When both "
"countries are choosed, a slider is displayed on which you can choose how "
"much armies there will be on each country afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid "Solution of the fight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To each army in the fight correspond a dice cast, a random number between 1 "
"and 6. The higher result of the attacker is opposed to the other one of the "
"defender. If the attacker's result is strictly higher than the defender one, "
"he wins the fight and the defender army is destroyed. Elsewhere, he looses "
"and its army is destroyed. The same happens for second higher dice of the "
"attacker if there is two or three attackers and two defenders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Attack result displayed</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Attack result displayed</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the number of armies in the defender country reaches 0, the ownership of "
"this country changes to the attacker: his flag is set up and one of his "
"attacking armies is installed in his new country. The \"Move armies\" slider "
"is displayed as for the moves of the end of the turn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Invasion slider</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Invasion slider</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "End of the turn"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To finish your current turn, if you don't want to move armies, you can hit "
"the \"Next Player\" button in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When everybody have played, the turn is finished. Some armies are "
"distributed to the players, in function of the coutries they own: 1 for each "
"group of three countries, with a minimum of 3. There is also a bonus for "
"players that own a complete continent, different for each one. This bonus is "
"of, fot the default skin:"
